      "subtitle": "A 5-day gentle journey for the woman in midlife — slowing, reweighing, longing for renewal — to discover that the deepest fruit is being grown precisely now",
      "goal": "A gentle 5-day journey for the woman between thirty-five and fifty-five who is feeling the quiet slowing of midlife — the body that does not bounce back the way it used to, the questions that have grown larger, the sense that the first half is closing and the second half is asking what it is for. Day by day we sit with five truths: the righteous still bring forth fruit in old age; the One who carried you from the womb will carry you to grey hairs; the inner woman is being renewed day by day even as the outer woman wears; the deep-rooted tree flourishes most in the dry season; and the treasure of Christ shines through, not in spite of, the cracks in the earthen vessel. By the end you will have written down three things you no longer want to spend your second half on, three things you do, and one specific way you will let yourself be renewed inwardly this week.",
