      "subtitle": "A 5-day gentle journey for the woman in the evening of her life — loosening her grip, considering her legacy, looking toward the blessed hope — to discover that her best years of usefulness are not behind her",
      "goal": "A gentle 5-day journey for the woman of fifty-five and beyond who has lived enough to know what truly matters, who is loosening her hands from what once felt urgent, who is asking what she will leave behind, and who is quietly looking toward the blessed hope. Day by day we sit with five truths: numbering our days teaches the heart wisdom; an unfeigned faith in one woman shapes generations to come; pressing forward is still the posture of the believer in her seventies and eighties; her later years are precisely when God wants to show His strength through her; and the blessed hope is the lamp that lights the rest of the road. By the end you will have written a one-page letter to the next generation, named one regret you are laying down, and named one specific way you intend to keep showing the Lord's strength this season.",
